  "releaseNotes": "- [ThunderPropagator.BuildingBlocks#10] DispatcherTimer.cs — both Run<TState> overloads:   - new Thread(Start).Start() → var _ = Task.Run(Start, CancellationToken.None) — uses ThreadPool instead of a raw OS thread   - async void Start() → async Task Start() — exceptions are now captured in the Task instead of silently swallowed   - Added try/catch (OperationCanceledException) { break; } around Task.Delay — clean loop exit on cancellation without the exception becoming an unobserved fault",
